Even federal law enforcement assisted in the investigation. Then, at 6.14pm, a call came through to 911. A panicked woman on the other line cried out, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I just want to go. The dispatcher tried to communicate with the caller, repeating the word hello several times. But the woman ignored her, instead talking to someone else nearby. It was a man. Why did you do that? he asked.
甚至联邦执法部门也协助了调查。然后，在下午6点14分，911接到一个电话。电话那头一个惊慌失措的女人哭喊道：“对不起，对不起，我只想走。”调度员试图与来电者沟通，重复了几次“喂”。但那个女人无视了她，转而与附近的人交谈。那是个男人。“你为什么要那样做？”他问。

9
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:43.000
The woman continued to apologize. She begged to be released and see her family. It sounded as though she and the man were in a moving vehicle. Her radio was playing music loudly in the background, making it difficult to hear what was going on. The dispatcher continued to ask questions which went ignored. The woman repeatedly begged to be let go. The man retorted, I was gonna let you go, then you go fuck around.
那个女人继续道歉。她恳求被释放并见见她的家人。听起来她和那个男人在一辆行驶的车辆中。她的收音机在背景中大声播放着音乐，让人很难听清发生了什么。调度员继续问问题，但都被忽略了。那个女人反复恳求被放走。那个男人反驳道：“我本来打算放你走的，结果你却乱搞。”

10
00:09:43.000 --> 00:10:19.000
He complained about having to drive a different route because she had done something, quote, in front of my cousin Harold. The dispatcher asked for an address while simultaneously putting a trace on the call. The woman asked the man where they were going. Didn't you see, the man responded. Exactly four streets, well five streets over from your house. The phone pinged off the North Port cell phone tower. The dispatcher asked for the woman's name.
他抱怨说不得不走另一条路，因为她做了某事，引用他的话，“在我的表弟哈罗德面前”。调度员要求提供地址，同时对电话进行追踪。那个女人问那个男人他们要去哪里。“你没看见吗？”那个男人回答道。“就在你家隔开四条街，哦不，五条街的地方。”电话信号定位到了北港的手机信号塔。调度员询问那个女人的名字。

11
00:10:19.000 --> 00:11:06.000
Please, my name is Denise, I'm married to a beautiful husband and I just want to see my kids again, she stated. It appeared as though she could hear the dispatcher, but had made the call discreetly and didn't want the man to realize. Her responses were phrased to mislead the man into thinking she was talking to him directly. What's your last name, the dispatcher asked. The woman responded, Lee. The man then seemingly caught on to the deception. He suddenly asked, what did you do with my cell phone? The car's radio stopped.
“求你了，我叫丹妮丝，我有一个很棒的丈夫，我只想再见到我的孩子们，”她说。看起来她能听到调度员的声音，但她是悄悄拨打的电话，不想让那个男人察觉。她的回答措辞是为了误导那个男人，让他以为她在直接对他说话。“你姓什么？”调度员问。那个女人回答：“李。”那个男人似乎识破了骗局。他突然问：“你对我的手机做了什么？”车里的收音机停了。

12
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:45.000
Right before the call abruptly disconnected, the woman was heard asking the man. The call lasted almost six minutes. Given Denise Lee's case was receiving wide-scale media and police attention, the possibility the call was a hoax was considered. The recording was played to Rick Goff, who immediately asked for the man's name. The call lasted almost six minutes. Unfortunately, the call was a hoax was considered. The recording was played to Rick Goff, who immediately identified the female caller as his daughter.
在电话突然断开之前，那个女人被听到在问那个男人。通话持续了近六分钟。鉴于丹妮丝·李的案件受到了媒体和警方的广泛关注，人们考虑了该电话是恶作剧的可能性。录音被播放给里克·戈夫听，他立即询问那个男人的名字。通话持续了近六分钟。不幸的是，人们考虑了该电话是恶作剧的可能性。录音被播放给里克·戈夫听，他立即认出那个女来电者是他的女儿。

13
00:11:45.000 --> 00:12:32.000
While devastating to hear her in trouble, the call offered Denise's loved ones a glimmer of hope. She was still alive. Authorities tried to trace the call, but it had been made using a cheap, prepaid phone. This meant it wasn't fitted with a GPS tracking device that investigators could use to pinpoint the phone's exact location. They could only uncover which towers it had pinged. However, they were able to identify the phone's owner via its number. It belonged to a 36-year-old unemployed plumber named Michael King. King had no criminal record aside from a few traffic fines.
虽然听到她陷入困境令人心碎，但这个电话给了丹妮丝的亲人一丝希望。她还活着。当局试图追踪电话，但它是用一部廉价的预付费手机拨打的。这意味着它没有配备调查人员可以用来精确定位手机确切位置的GPS追踪装置。他们只能查出它连接了哪些信号塔。然而，他们能够通过号码识别出手机的主人。它属于一名36岁、失业的管道工，名叫迈克尔·金。金除了几张交通罚单外，没有犯罪记录。

14
00:12:32.000 --> 00:13:23.000
The name meant nothing to Denise's family. They had no idea who Michael King was and couldn't imagine why he would target Denise. Harold Muxlow lived on Carlec Street, about four miles south of the Lee's home. He was completely unaware of the investigation unfolding nearby. Sometime between 5.30 and 6.00 pm, Harold heard a knock at his front door. It was his cousin, 36-year-old Michael King. Michael explained that his lawn mower had become stuck in his yard and he needed some equipment to dig it out. He asked to borrow a shovel, a gas can and a flashlight.
这个名字对丹妮丝的家人来说毫无意义。他们不知道迈克尔·金是谁，也无法想象他为什么要针对丹妮丝。哈罗德·马克斯洛住在卡莱克街，距离李家以南约四英里。他完全不知道附近正在进行的调查。下午5点30分到6点之间，哈罗德听到有人敲前门。是他的表弟，36岁的迈克尔·金。迈克尔解释说他的割草机卡在院子里了，需要一些工具把它挖出来。他借了一把铲子、一个汽油桶和一把手电筒。

15
00:13:23.000 --> 00:14:01.000
Harold invited Michael inside. The two men chatted for a while before Harold handed the tools over. Michael then carried them over to his green Chevrolet Camaro and said goodbye to his cousin. As Harold turned to walk back inside, he heard a woman's voice scream, called the cops. The plea had come from inside Michael's vehicle. Harold spun around. What the fuck are you doing? He asked Michael. Nothing, his cousin replied. Don't worry about it.
哈罗德请迈克尔进屋。两人聊了一会儿，哈罗德把工具交给了他。迈克尔随后把它们搬到他的绿色雪佛兰科迈罗上，并向他的表弟告别。当哈罗德转身走回屋里时，他听到一个女人的声音尖叫道：“报警！”这个请求来自迈克尔的车内。哈罗德猛地转过身。“你到底在干什么？”他问迈克尔。“没什么，”他表弟回答。“别担心。”

16
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:45.000
Don't worry about it. Harold figured Michael was having an argument with a girlfriend. Michael had been known to have some tempestuous relationships since his marriage ended almost seven years earlier. Harold began to walk towards his house, but his curiosity got the better of him. He turned around and headed back down the driveway towards Michael's car. He could see a female silhouette with shoulder length hair in the back seat. It was too dim to see any of her other features. Michael had clambered into the car and was crawling over the console.
“别担心。”哈罗德以为迈克尔在和女朋友吵架。众所周知，自七年前婚姻结束以来，迈克尔有一些动荡的关系。哈罗德开始朝他的房子走去，但好奇心战胜了他。他转过身，沿着车道朝迈克尔的车走去。他可以看到后座上有一个留着齐肩长发的女性轮廓。光线太暗，看不清她的其他特征。迈克尔爬进车里，正爬过中控台。

17
00:14:45.000 --> 00:15:38.000
He pushed the woman's head down so she was out of sight. One of the woman's knees rose up as though she was struggling against Michael. Michael then climbed back into the driver's seat, started the engine and drove away. Harold Muxlow wasn't sure what to do. He wasn't certain that anything was seriously wrong, but the incident didn't sit right with him. He decided to drive over to Michael's house to see if his story checked out. If he found Michael there and the lawnmower was indeed stuck in his yard, then Harold would know his cousin had been telling the truth. Michael only lived about six miles away in another part of Northport, so it didn't take Harold long to drive over.
他把那个女人的头按下去，让她看不见。那个女人的膝盖抬了起来，好像在和迈克尔挣扎。迈克尔随后爬回驾驶座，发动引擎开走了。哈罗德·马克斯洛不知道该怎么办。他不确定是否真的出了什么严重的问题，但这件事让他感觉不对劲。他决定开车去迈克尔家看看他的说法是否属实。如果他在那里找到了迈克尔，而且割草机确实卡在院子里，那么哈罗德就会知道他表弟说的是实话。迈克尔只住在约六英里外的北港另一部分，所以哈罗德没花多久就开车到了那里。

18
00:15:38.000 --> 00:16:29.000
Michael's Camaro wasn't parked in the driveway, and when Harold rang the doorbell, no one answered. There wasn't a lawnmower in sight. Harold was reluctant to alert the authorities. Instead, he phoned his 17-year-old daughter Sabrina and informed her of what had taken place. Harold told Sabrina not to call the police, but as soon as they entered their call, Sabrina didn't hesitate. She phoned 911 at 6.23pm, just minutes after the frantic call placed by Denise Lee. Realising the significance of Sabrina's call, the dispatcher said, You are just so wonderful to call us and give us this information.
迈克尔的科迈罗没有停在车道上，当哈罗德按门铃时，没有人回答。视线内没有割草机。哈罗德不愿惊动当局。相反，他给17岁的女儿萨布丽娜打了电话，告诉她发生了什么事。哈罗德告诉萨布丽娜不要报警，但他们刚挂断电话，萨布丽娜就毫不犹豫地拨打了911，时间是下午6点23分，就在丹妮丝·李拨出那个疯狂电话的几分钟后。意识到萨布丽娜电话的重要性，调度员说：“你打电话给我们并提供这些信息真是太棒了。”

19
