00:32:34.000 --> 00:33:23.000
Fran's family members and former colleagues described him as a nice guy who was happy go lucky. He didn't drink or do drugs, had no history of domestic violence, and was regarded as a hard worker. But he had experienced some misfortune. Originally from Michigan, King was in a sledding accident at age six and suffered a head injury. His family said he changed after that. He suffered headaches which were exacerbated by stress. He struggled at school and had to repeat the first grade. By the time King was eight, he still couldn't write all the letters in the alphabet. A social worker recommended he enter a special education program.
弗兰的家人和前同事形容他是一个快乐、随和的好人。他不喝酒也不吸毒，没有家庭暴力史，被认为是一个勤奋的人。但他经历了一些不幸。金来自密歇根州，6岁时发生了一起雪橇事故，头部受伤。他的家人说他从那以后就变了。他患有头痛，压力会加剧头痛。他在学校表现挣扎，不得不留级一年级。到金8岁时，他仍然无法写出字母表中的所有字母。一名社会工作者建议他参加特殊教育项目。

39
00:33:23.000 --> 00:34:10.000
King also became more impulsive after the accident. When he was 13, he decided to act out a scene from a cartoon that featured a bow and arrow. He nearly killed his brother in the process. At 17, he saw the Texas train saw massacre. Imitating the film's villain Leatherface, King acquired a chainsaw. He began chasing family members with it. His facial expression entirely blank. But King found a vocation in plumbing, got married and had two children. In March 2001, King had been almost 30 years old when he came home from work one day to discover his wife was missing.
事故发生后，金也变得更加冲动。13岁时，他决定表演一个卡通片里的场景，里面有弓和箭。他差点在过程中杀死了他的兄弟。17岁时，他看了《德州电锯杀人狂》。模仿电影里的反派“人皮脸”，金弄到了一把电锯。他开始用它追赶家人。他的面部表情完全空白。但金在管道行业找到了职业，结婚并有了两个孩子。2001年3月，金快30岁时，有一天下班回家发现妻子失踪了。

40
00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:59.000
King went to the local sheriff's department and filed a missing persons report. It soon emerged that his wife was safe and well. She had left King for another man who she'd met on the internet. The couple divorced and King received full-time custody of their son. His wife retained custody of their other child. King purchased the three-bedroom house on Sardinia Avenue and had a series of romantic relationships with different women. Not long after King moved into his house, a feud broke out between him and his next door neighbor. She accused his son of damaging her family's inflatable pool.
金去了当地警长部门并提交了一份失踪人员报告。很快发现他的妻子平安无事。她为了另一个在互联网上认识的男人离开了金。这对夫妇离婚了，金获得了他们儿子的全职监护权。他的妻子保留了他们另一个孩子的监护权。金购买了萨丁尼亚大道上的那栋三居室房子，并与不同的女性有过一系列浪漫关系。金搬进房子后不久，他和隔壁邻居之间就爆发了争执。她指责他的儿子损坏了她家人的充气游泳池。

41
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:45.000
The neighbor installed a wooden fence between the two properties which upset King. He reportedly took revenge by keying the neighbor's car, slashing its tires, pouring battery acid on her pool cage and throwing eggs at her. The neighbor filed reports with Northport Police. King denied the allegations and there was no evidence against him. Others in the area also disliked King. He was known to deliberately screech his tires loudly as he drove. Some said he would walk around the neighborhood alone at night, peeping into people's windows. King was alleged to have exposed himself to one woman outside a hair salon.
邻居在两处房产之间安装了木栅栏，这让金很不高兴。据报道，他通过划伤邻居的车、割破轮胎、在她的泳池笼上泼电池酸以及向她扔鸡蛋来进行报复。邻居向北港警方提交了报告。金否认了这些指控，也没有证据对他不利。该地区的其他人也不喜欢金。众所周知，他开车时会故意大声刺耳地刹车。有人说他会在晚上独自在社区里走动，窥视人们的窗户。据称，金在一家美发沙龙外向一名女性暴露自己。

42
00:35:45.000 --> 00:36:27.000
Another woman said he had raped her. Neither of these incidents resulted in any charges. For four years, King worked at the same plumbing company until he abruptly left in June 2007. His boss would later tell police King was a habitual liar. He and his 13-year-old son travelled back to Michigan that same month. King's house in Northport sat empty and unoccupied for five years. King's house in Northport sat empty and unoccupied for months. By December 2007, his lack of steady income meant he was facing bankruptcy and foreclosure on his home.
另一名女性说他强奸了她。这些事件都没有导致任何指控。四年来，金在同一家管道公司工作，直到2007年6月突然离开。他的老板后来告诉警察，金是一个惯性说谎者。他和13岁的儿子在同一个月回到了密歇根州。金在北港的房子空置了五个月。金在北港的房子空置了几个月。到2007年12月，他缺乏稳定的收入意味着他面临破产和房屋止赎。

43
00:36:27.000 --> 00:37:20.000
He also broke up with a girlfriend. At the beginning of 2008, he returned to Florida in the hope of sorting out his financial problems and keeping his house. Family members said King began acting oddly around this time, as though he were dazed or even catatonic. He also seemed paranoid. On Sunday, January 13, 2008, less than a week before Denise Amberlee was abducted, other residents on Sardinia Avenue suddenly saw Michael King at his home again. He was with a blonde woman his neighbours didn't recognise. This was likely his new girlfriend, who later told investigators that King's behaviour had been growing even more extreme.
他还和女朋友分手了。2008年初，他回到佛罗里达，希望能解决他的财务问题并保住他的房子。家人说金在这段时间开始表现得很奇怪，好像他处于恍惚甚至紧张性精神症状态。他也显得很偏执。2008年1月13日星期日，在丹妮丝·安布尔·李被绑架前不到一周，萨丁尼亚大道上的其他居民突然又看到了迈克尔·金在家。他和一名邻居不认识的金发女子在一起。这很可能是他的新女朋友，她后来告诉调查人员，金的行为变得越来越极端。

44
00:37:20.000 --> 00:38:12.000
Two days before he took Denise, he told his girlfriend that he thought the neighbours were spying through his windows. He also allegedly owned a 9mm handgun. Investigators couldn't find the gun anywhere, or find any evidence of its existence. It was suspected King had disposed of it at some stage. No ammunition was ever found in his possession either. Despite the lack of a murder weapon, investigators had forensic evidence tying Michael King to Denise Lee, as well as multiple eyewitnesses and circumstantial evidence. King was charged with first degree murder and involuntary sexual battery in addition to the kidnapping charge.
在他带走丹妮丝的两天前，他告诉女朋友，他认为邻居在通过他的窗户监视他。他还据称拥有一把9毫米手枪。调查人员在任何地方都找不到这把枪，也找不到任何证据证明它的存在。人们怀疑金在某个阶段处理掉了它。在他身上也没有发现任何弹药。尽管缺乏凶器，但调查人员有法医证据将迈克尔·金与丹妮丝·李联系起来，以及多名目击者和间接证据。除了绑架指控外，金还被控一级谋杀和非自愿性暴力。

45
00:38:12.000 --> 00:39:12.000
Michael King's trial began in late August 2009, more than 18 months after Denise Amberlee's abduction and murder. The prosecution didn't know how or why King had targeted Denise. When a member of the public reported seeing both Denise and King at the same post office earlier on the day of the attack, it was theorised that King had followed Denise home from there. But this sighting was later debunked as mistaken. A woman who lived in the same street as Denise Lee thought she recognised King as a plumber who'd come to look at her house when it was for sale the previous summer. With no confirmed link between the two, it was posited that King had simply trawled the neighbourhood looking for a victim. For some reason he had chosen Denise and gained access to her home while she was there alone with her two young sons.
迈克尔·金的审判于2009年8月下旬开始，距离丹妮丝·安布尔·李被绑架和谋杀已经过去了18个多月。检方不知道金是如何以及为什么针对丹妮丝的。当一名公众报告说在袭击当天早些时候在同一个邮局看到了丹妮丝和金时，人们推测金是从那里跟踪丹妮丝回家的。但这一目击事件后来被证明是错误的。一位住在丹妮丝·李同一条街上的女人以为她认出金是去年夏天她家出售时来看房的管道工。由于两人之间没有确凿的联系，人们推测金只是在社区里游荡寻找受害者。出于某种原因，他选择了丹妮丝，并在她独自带着两个年幼儿子在家时进入了她的家。

46
00:39:12.000 --> 00:40:23.000
Nathan Lee noted that King's 1995 green Camaro looked very similar to the 1995 green Dodge Avenger he drove. Perhaps when Michael King pulled into their driveway, Denise had mistaken him for her husband. Upon realising she was in danger, she kept her children safe by placing them together in a cot in their bedroom. She then hurriedly closed all the windows and locked the front door. The prosecution had plenty of physical and DNA evidence to back up their case, including the silver ring and strands of hair they believed Denise had deliberately left in King's car. Numerous witnesses who could place Denise in King's car also testified for the prosecution, including King's cousin Harold Muxlow. All of the 911 calls received that night were played for the court, including the one Denise had made herself. Harold Muxlow confirmed that the male voice on Denise's call was Michael King.
内森·李指出，金1995年的绿色科迈罗看起来和他驾驶的1995年绿色道奇复仇者非常相似。也许当迈克尔·金驶入他们的车道时，丹妮丝误把他当成了自己的丈夫。意识到自己处于危险之中后，她把孩子们放在卧室的婴儿床里，以确保他们的安全。随后，她匆忙关上所有窗户并锁上了前门。检方有大量的物证和DNA证据支持他们的案件，包括他们认为丹妮丝故意留在金车里的银戒指和几缕头发。多名能证明丹妮丝在金车里的证人也为检方作证，其中包括金的表弟哈罗德·穆克斯洛。当晚接到的所有911报警电话都在法庭上进行了播放，包括丹妮丝自己打的那通。哈罗德·穆克斯洛证实，丹妮丝通话中出现的男性声音就是迈克尔·金。

47
00:40:23.000 --> 00:41:17.000
The defence didn't call any witnesses, instead they tried to implicate a friend of King's named Robert Salvador. Police initially thought Robert was King's accomplice after they learnt the two were together shortly before Denise lays abduction. They had gone to a gun range that morning to practise target shooting. King brought along a 9mm handgun while Robert supplied the ammunition. They finished at 1pm, around 90 minutes before Denise was taken. Robert had alibis confirming that he wasn't with King during or after her abduction. The defence attempted to place the pair together when Denise was killed and accused Robert of executing her. Robert vehemently denied this.
辩方没有传唤任何证人，而是试图牵连金的一位名叫罗伯特·萨尔瓦多的朋友。警方最初认为罗伯特是金的同伙，因为他们得知两人在丹妮丝被绑架前不久曾在一起。那天早上他们去了一个射击场练习打靶。金带了一把9毫米手枪，而罗伯特提供了弹药。他们在下午1点结束，大约在丹妮丝被带走前90分钟。罗伯特有不在场证明，证实他在丹妮丝被绑架期间或之后并没有和金在一起。辩方试图将两人在丹妮丝遇害时联系在一起，并指控罗伯特是行凶者。罗伯特对此予以强烈否认。

48
00:41:17.000 --> 00:42:03.000
The judge subsequently instructed the jury to dismiss several of these questions, stating, There is no basis in fact from the evidence for the asking of these questions. The jury deliberated for two hours before reaching a verdict. Guilty on all counts. Denise's husband, parents, her 20 year old sister and 15 year old brother all cried as it was delivered. King stared straight ahead. The jury also recommended he receive a death sentence. It was a sentence Denise's family were in favour of.
法官随后指示陪审团驳回其中几个问题，称：“这些问题的提出在证据基础上没有任何事实依据。”陪审团经过两个小时的审议后达成裁决：所有罪名成立。丹妮丝的丈夫、父母、20岁的姐姐和15岁的弟弟在宣判时都哭了。金直视前方。陪审团还建议判处他死刑。这是丹妮丝家人所支持的判决。

49
00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:57.000
Nathan Lee told the Tampa Tribune, quote, One thing that really bothers me is he can think about Denise whenever he wants to. I don't want him to have those memories. I want him gone. A penalty phase was held to determine whether King was competent to receive a death sentence. The defence argued that the sledding accident he'd suffered as a six year old caused permanent brain damage. A psychiatrist who performed a scan on King said his frontal lobe showed indications of abnormal activity consistent with a traumatic brain injury. He explained that individuals with frontal lobe injuries can sometimes exhibit poor judgement, risk taking behaviour and poor impulse control.
内森·李告诉《坦帕论坛报》：“有一件事真的很困扰我，那就是他想什么时候想起丹妮丝就可以什么时候想起。我不希望他拥有那些记忆。我希望他消失。”法庭举行了量刑阶段听证会，以确定金是否有能力接受死刑判决。辩方辩称，他六岁时遭受的雪橇事故导致了永久性脑损伤。一位对金进行扫描的精神科医生表示，他的额叶显示出与创伤性脑损伤一致的异常活动迹象。他解释说，额叶受伤的人有时会表现出判断力差、冒险行为和冲动控制能力差的问题。

50
00:42:57.000 --> 00:44:01.000
King's siblings testified about some of his dangerous behaviour as an adolescent. The psychiatrist also said that a recent verbal IQ score King had taken placed him in the borderline range of having an intellectual disability. The prosecution's expert psychologist also had King take an IQ test. While his results also placed King in the borderline range, he counted that King's ability to concentrate and comprehend was stronger than the results indicated. The trial judge ruled that King was competent and sentenced him to death by lethal injection for the murder of Denise Amber Lee. King later appealed his conviction but it was upheld. As of late 2022 he remains on death row in Florida. The conviction of Michael King wasn't the end of the Denise Amber Lee case.
金的兄弟姐妹作证说他青少年时期有一些危险行为。精神科医生还表示，金最近进行的言语智商测试得分处于智力残疾的边缘范围。检方的专家心理学家也让金参加了智商测试。虽然结果也显示金处于边缘范围，但他反驳说，金的专注和理解能力比结果显示的要强。审判法官裁定金具有完全行为能力，并因谋杀丹妮丝·安珀·李判处他注射死刑。金后来对定罪提出上诉，但被驳回。截至2022年底，他仍被关押在佛罗里达州的死囚牢房中。迈克尔·金的定罪并不是丹妮丝·安珀·李案件的终结。

51
00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:54.000
Many questions remained as to whether she could have been saved given the number of 911 calls received as the crime was taking place. Particularly significant was the 911 call from witness Jane Kowalski. She provided real-time updates to emergency dispatch while attempting to follow King's Camaro along US Highway 41. She also gave the dispatcher her contact information in case anything further was required. Jane didn't hear back from law enforcement after making her call. The following day she saw news footage of Michael King's arrest. She recognized him immediately as the driver of the Camaro she'd seen. At the time, Jane believed she was witnessing a child abduction.
关于在犯罪发生时接到如此多911报警电话的情况下，她是否本可以获救，仍存在许多疑问。其中特别重要的是目击者简·科瓦尔斯基打来的911电话。她在试图沿着41号美国国道追踪金的科迈罗时，向紧急调度员提供了实时更新。她还向调度员提供了自己的联系方式，以防需要进一步的信息。简在打完电话后没有收到执法部门的回复。第二天，她看到了迈克尔·金被捕的新闻片段。她立刻认出他就是她看到的科迈罗的司机。当时，简以为自己目睹了一起儿童绑架案。

52
00:44:54.000 --> 00:45:40.000
It wasn't until then she discovered King had actually taken a grown woman. Jane told the television program Dateline of her distress upon realizing the crime had been real. She decided to call the North Port Police Department telling them, I'm the 911 caller who called in. Do you need any more information from me? The North Port Police were baffled. They had no idea what Jane was referring to and had no record of her call. Because of Jane's location when she rang, her call had been routed to neighboring Charlotte County, not Sarasota County where North Port was situated.
直到那时她才发现金实际上带走的是一名成年女性。简在电视节目《日界线》中讲述了她在意识到犯罪是真实发生时的痛苦。她决定致电北港警察局，告诉他们：“我是那个打911报警的人。你们还需要我提供更多信息吗？”北港警方感到困惑。他们根本不知道简在说什么，也没有她报警的记录。由于简拨打电话时所处的位置，她的电话被转接到了邻近的夏洛特县，而不是北港所在的萨拉索塔县。

53
00:45:40.000 --> 00:46:34.000
For some reason, Charlotte County Sheriff's Department, the same department that Denise's father worked for, had failed to pass the message along. An internal investigation revealed that the 911 operator who'd taken the call realized it was related to the Denise Amperley case and had been urgent. However, she hadn't entered the information into a computer database as per protocol. Instead, she'd called it out to police dispatchers who sat across the aisle from her and passed over a handwritten note. They heard her but hadn't sent the tip out due to the particularly chaotic circumstances of that night. One dispatcher thought she couldn't send it out due to mistakenly thinking her radio wasn't working.
出于某种原因，夏洛特县治安官部门——也就是丹妮丝父亲工作的同一个部门——未能传递这条信息。内部调查显示，接听电话的911接线员意识到这与丹妮丝·安珀·李案有关，而且情况紧急。然而，她并没有按照规定将信息输入计算机数据库。相反，她把它喊给了坐在她过道对面的警察调度员，并递过一张手写纸条。他们听到了她的喊话，但由于当晚情况特别混乱，没有发出警报。一名调度员认为她无法发出警报，因为她错误地以为自己的无线电坏了。

54
00:46:34.000 --> 00:47:34.000
Others assumed their colleagues passed it along. Jane Kowalski's crucial information had simply slipped through the cracks. At the time, multiple sheriff's deputies had been stationed along the road that Michael King was driving along while Denise was still alive in the back seat. One deputy realized he had likely been stationed at the Toledo Blade Boulevard intersection at 6.35pm, around the same time that King drove through it. Without the tip-off being passed along, he hadn't noticed King's car. The investigation led to the call operator requesting a voluntary demotion to a desk clerk position after 15 years in the job. Four call operators had to undergo remedial training. Two dispatchers were suspended for failing to send out patrol cars in response to the call.
其他人则以为同事已经传达了。简·科瓦尔斯基的关键信息就这样被遗漏了。当时，多名治安官副手就驻扎在迈克尔·金驾驶的道路沿线，而丹妮丝当时还活着，就在后座上。一名副手意识到他当时很可能就在下午6点35分驻扎在托莱多刀锋大道交叉口，大约就在金开车经过的时间。由于没有收到提示，他没有注意到金的车。调查导致该接线员在工作15年后主动申请降职为文员。四名接线员不得不接受补救培训。两名调度员因未能响应报警电话派出巡逻车而被停职。

55
00:47:34.000 --> 00:48:49.000
One for 60 hours and the other for 36. While the Charlotte County Sheriff publicly announced the suspensions, he did not apologize for the errors. Denise's father, Rick Goff, has struggled with the knowledge that such a mistake was made by the same department he'd spent 25 years working for. She's beating on the window so hard and screaming trying to get help, which is the smart thing to do because by that time she knows she probably wasn't coming back, he told television program Dateline. As far as I'm concerned, we blew it. And I say we, because I'm part of that sheriff's office. Rick began to lobby for improved training for 911 call takers, which led to the Denise Amberley Act being signed into Florida law. The Act provides for voluntary training for emergency line operators. Rick and other members of Denise's family continue to advocate for mandatory training and certification for all 911 operators.
一人被停职60小时，另一人被停职36小时。虽然夏洛特县治安官公开宣布了停职决定，但他并没有为这些错误道歉。丹妮丝的父亲里克·戈夫一直为这样一个事实感到痛苦：这个错误竟然是由他工作了25年的同一个部门犯下的。他告诉电视节目《日界线》：“她当时拼命拍打窗户并尖叫着寻求帮助，这是明智的做法，因为那时她知道自己可能回不来了。就我而言，我们搞砸了。我说‘我们’，是因为我也是治安官办公室的一员。”里克开始游说改进911接线员的培训，这促使《丹妮丝·安珀·李法案》被签署成为佛罗里达州法律。该法案规定为紧急线路接线员提供自愿培训。里克和丹妮丝家人的其他成员继续倡导对所有911接线员进行强制性培训和认证。

56
00:48:49.000 --> 00:49:50.000
Nathan Lee told Dateline that if Janka Wolskie's information had been passed on, quote, There's not a doubt in my mind Denise would still be here. Not a doubt in my mind. In the wake of his wife's murder, Nathan found it difficult to return to his job as a meter reader. The position gave him too much time to walk and think. He found the constant rumination painful. Six months after his wife's death, Nathan established the Denise Amberley Foundation to advocate for improvements to the 911 system. The nonprofit was a way to create some good for his family's enormous loss by using their tragedy to impart valuable lessons. Nathan has traveled all over the United States to share Denise's story with call takers. Speaking on 911 reform is now his full-time career.
内森·李告诉《日界线》，如果简·科瓦尔斯基的信息被传达出去，“我毫不怀疑丹妮丝现在还会在这里。我对此深信不疑。”在妻子遇害后，内森发现很难回到他担任抄表员的工作岗位。这份工作给了他太多走路和思考的时间。他发现不断的沉思非常痛苦。在妻子去世六个月后，内森成立了丹妮丝·安珀·李基金会，以倡导改进911系统。这个非营利组织是一种通过利用他们的悲剧来传授宝贵经验，从而为他家人的巨大损失创造一些积极意义的方式。内森走遍了美国各地，与接线员分享丹妮丝的故事。现在，就911改革进行演讲已成为他的全职工作。

